@startuml dynamic_discovery
title Dynamic Discovery & Autonomous Delegation

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFCC

' ==================== THE PROBLEM ====================
package "The Challenge" as challenge #LightCoral {
    note as problemNote
      **Pre-defined workflows don't work here!**

      Traditional approach:
      <code>
      if needs_containerization:
          call_agent_b()
      </code>

      **Problem:** We don't know in advance
      what issues will be discovered.

      The "need for containerization" emerges
      during Claude's reasoning process.
    end note
}

' ==================== THE SOLUTION ====================
package "Solution: Claude Self-Reporting" as solution #LightGreen {
    note as solutionNote
      **Claude Code has built-in awareness:**

      During execution, Claude can recognize:
      • "This code won't work in production as-is"
      • "I'm not the right expert for this subtask"
      • "This requires different skills/tools"

      **Claude autonomously decides to:**
      1. Report the discovery
      2. Request collaboration
      3. Continue with what it CAN do
    end note
}

' ==================== IMPLEMENTATION ====================
package "Implementation Options" as impl #LightBlue {

    package "Option 1: Tool-Based Reporting" as opt1 {
        note as opt1Note
          **Give Claude a "request_help" tool:**
          <code>
          @tool
          def request_collaboration(
              issue: str,
              expertise_needed: str,
              context: dict
          ) -> str:
              """Request another agent's help"""
              return orchestrator.delegate(
                  issue, expertise_needed, context
              )
          </code>

          Claude calls this when it discovers
          something outside its expertise.
        end note
    }

    package "Option 2: System Prompt" as opt2 {
        note as opt2Note
          **Instruct Claude in system prompt:**

          "When you discover a task that requires
          different expertise (DevOps, Security, etc.),
          use the request_collaboration() tool to
          delegate. Do not try to do everything yourself.

          Examples of when to delegate:
          - Containerization → DevOps agent
          - Security review → Security agent
          - Database design → DBA agent"
        end note
    }

    package "Option 3: Reflection Loop" as opt3 {
        note as opt3Note
          **Periodic self-check:**
          <code>
          while working:
              result = claude.step()
              
              # Ask Claude to reflect
              reflection = claude.ask(
                  "Do you need help from
                   another specialist?"
              )
              
              if reflection.needs_help:
                  delegate(reflection.task)
          </code>
        end note
    }
}

' ==================== CONCRETE EXAMPLE ====================
package "Your Example: Data Download → Containerization" as example #Lavender {
    note as exampleNote
      **Timeline:**

      1. User: "Implement data download feature"

      2. Agent A (Claude Code) starts working...
         - Writing download logic ✓
         - Adding error handling ✓
         - Writing tests ✓

      3. **Discovery moment:**
         Claude thinks: "Wait, this uses local file paths.
         For production, this needs to run in a container
         with proper volume mounts. I should ask a DevOps
         agent to handle the containerization."

      4. Agent A calls:
         <code>
         request_collaboration(
             issue="needs_containerization",
             expertise_needed="devops",
             context={
                 "code": current_code,
                 "reason": "production deployment needs
                           container with volume mounts",
                 "requirements": ["Dockerfile", "docker-compose"]
             }
         )
         </code>

      5. Agent A continues working on other parts
         (API endpoints, documentation, etc.)

      6. Agent B (DevOps) receives task, creates:
         - Dockerfile
         - docker-compose.yml
         - CI/CD pipeline

      7. Agent A receives notification, integrates result

      8. Feature complete with containerization!
    end note
}

' ==================== KEY INSIGHT ====================
package "Key Insight" as insight #Gold {
    note as insightNote
      **The magic is in Claude's reasoning:**

      Claude doesn't follow a pre-defined flowchart.
      It THINKS about the problem and RECOGNIZES
      when it needs help.

      This is why multi-agent systems with LLMs
      are different from traditional microservices:

      | Traditional | LLM Agents |
      |-------------|------------|
      | Pre-defined rules | Emergent behavior |
      | if/else logic | Reasoning |
      | Static workflow | Dynamic collaboration |
    end note
}

@enduml
